# XSH statvfs
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
# statvfs() and fstatvfs() share this page. The page says it is unspecified
# whether all structure members have meaningful values, so no relation between
# block counts is required; the test compare members that stay put between two
# calls (f_bsize, f_frsize, f_fsid, f_flag, f_namemax); counts that
# may change with use (blocks, file serial numbers) are not compared.
# Errors that need a failing disk (EIO), a signal (EINTR) or a value too large
# (EOVERFLOW) are not tested.

assertion  XSH.statvfs.001
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of "." and of a regular file, and fstatvfs() of a descriptor of
           that file, return 0, and the members f_bsize, f_frsize, f_fsid, f_flag and
           f_namemax are the same from the three calls (one file system).
test       t/001-both-succeed.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.002
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of a regular file with mode 0 succeeds for a process without
           privileges, and fstatvfs() of a descriptor opened on that file before its
           mode was cleared succeeds.
test       t/002-no-permission.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.003
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       If f_flag has ST_RDONLY, creating a file in the working directory fails
           with EROFS; if it has not, creating one succeeds.
test       t/003-rdonly-flag.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.004
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2008
says       fstatvfs() of -1 and of a closed descriptor fails with EBADF.
test       t/004-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.005
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#ERRORS/ENOENT
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of a missing name and of the empty string fails with ENOENT.
test       t/005-enoent.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.006
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#ERRORS/ENOTDIR
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of "f/x" and of "f/", where f is a regular file, fails with
           ENOTDIR.
test       t/006-enotdir.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.007
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#ERRORS/ENAMETOOLONG
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of a name whose component is longer than {NAME_MAX} fails with
           ENAMETOOLONG.
test       t/007-enametoolong.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.008
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#ERRORS/EACCES
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of d/f where d denies search permission fails with EACCES for a
           process without privileges.
test       t/008-eacces.c

assertion  XSH.statvfs.009
anchor     functions/statvfs.html#ERRORS/ELOOP
class      required
since      2008
says       statvfs() of a symbolic link that points at itself fails with ELOOP.
test       t/009-eloop.c
